<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Complete DSR heatmaps across all evaluated models showing defense performance against 20 jailbreak attack methods. <span id="A2.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SIRL</span> consistently achieves the highest defense rates across all models and attack types.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Consistency Across Different LLM Judges</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the robustness of our safety evaluation, we assessed model responses using three different LLM judges: rule-based GCG detection, Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct, and Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct. Figures <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ B.2 Consistency Across Different LLM Judges ‣ Appendix B Extended Results ‣ Safety Instincts: LLMs Learn to Trust Their Internal Compass for Self-Defense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B.2 Consistency Across Different LLM Judges ‣ Appendix B Extended Results ‣ Safety Instincts: LLMs Learn to Trust Their Internal Compass for Self-Defense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, and <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ B.2 Consistency Across Different LLM Judges ‣ Appendix B Extended Results ‣ Safety Instincts: LLMs Learn to Trust Their Internal Compass for Self-Defense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> presents comprehensive DSR heatmaps using each judge across all four evaluated models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
